<div class="pulse-auth-page">
  <div class="pulse-auth-success">
    <h1 class="pulse-auth-title">Your account is scheduled for deletion</h1>
    <p class="pulse-auth-subtitle">
      It will be permanently deleted on <strong><%= @scrub_date.to_date.to_fs(:long) %></strong>.
      Until then, you can restore it.
    </p>
    <ul style="text-align:left; margin: 16px 0; line-height: 1.6;">
      <li>On the deletion date, your profile is anonymized and your access is permanently removed. Content you shared stays, attributed to "Deleted User".</li>
      <li>If you have a prepaid balance, it is forfeited on the deletion date — not before.</li>
      <li>Your API tokens were revoked and your plan subscription was cancelled when you requested deletion. After restoring, issue new tokens and restart the subscription if you want paid features.</li>
      <li>Restoring re-enables your automations and your agents.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="pulse-form-actions" style="justify-content:center;">
      <%= button_to "Restore my account", account_deletion_restore_path, method: :post, class: "pulse-action-btn" %>
    </div>
    <div class="pulse-form-actions" style="justify-content:center; margin-top: 8px;">
      <%= button_to "Log out", "/logout", method: :delete, class: "pulse-action-btn-subtle" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
